1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,899
Tie a pen to the tyre valve, then pull
a long sheet of paper past the turning

2
00:00:04,899 --> 00:00:05,799
wheel.

3
00:00:05,839 --> 00:00:07,678
What shape will the pen draw?

4
00:00:07,678 --> 00:00:08,578
A circle?

5
00:00:08,410 --> 00:00:09,310
A zigzag?

6
00:00:09,543 --> 00:00:12,657
Aarav pictured this while
riding home from college.

7
00:00:13,007 --> 00:00:17,393
The valve goes up and down, again and
again, while the paper keeps sliding.

8
00:00:17,893 --> 00:00:19,745
The pen draws a smooth wave.

9
00:00:19,745 --> 00:00:21,791
That wave is the graph of sine.

10
00:00:21,791 --> 00:00:23,929
Today we draw it, and two more.

11
00:00:24,579 --> 00:00:25,984
Here is the rule.

12
00:00:25,984 --> 00:00:29,864
The angle x goes along the
horizontal axis, in radians.

13
00:00:29,864 --> 00:00:33,167
The value of sine x goes
up the vertical axis.

14
00:00:33,567 --> 00:00:35,767
Now turn P round the unit circle.

15
00:00:35,767 --> 00:00:37,284
Its height is sine x.

16
00:00:37,284 --> 00:00:39,720
Carry that height across to the graph.

17
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:42,057
At zero, the height is zero.

18
00:00:42,057 --> 00:00:44,710
At pi by two, it reaches one, the top.

19
00:00:45,110 --> 00:00:46,698
At pi, back to zero.

20
00:00:46,698 --> 00:00:50,174
At three pi by two, down
to minus one, the bottom.

21
00:00:50,574 --> 00:00:53,957
At two pi, P is home, and
the height is zero again.

22
00:00:53,957 --> 00:00:57,131
Join the points smoothly,
and the sine wave appears.

23
00:00:57,781 --> 00:01:00,448
Five key points are all
you need to sketch it.

24
00:01:00,798 --> 00:01:01,698
Step one.

25
00:01:01,684 --> 00:01:04,190
At x equals zero, sine is zero.

26
00:01:04,190 --> 00:01:06,469
The wave starts at the origin.

27
00:01:07,219 --> 00:01:08,119
Step two.

28
00:01:08,017 --> 00:01:10,029
At pi by two, sine is one.

29
00:01:10,029 --> 00:01:11,828
That is the highest point.

30
00:01:12,578 --> 00:01:13,555
Step three.

31
00:01:13,555 --> 00:01:15,306
At pi, sine is zero.

32
00:01:15,306 --> 00:01:18,374
The wave crosses the axis on its way down.

33
00:01:19,124 --> 00:01:20,024
Step four.

34
00:01:19,992 --> 00:01:23,956
At three pi by two, sine is
minus one, the lowest point.

35
00:01:23,956 --> 00:01:26,283
At two pi, it is back to zero.

36
00:01:27,033 --> 00:01:31,529
After two pi, P simply goes round
again, so the same wave repeats.

37
00:01:31,529 --> 00:01:33,316
That is the next episode.

38
00:01:33,966 --> 00:01:35,037
Now cosine.

39
00:01:35,037 --> 00:01:38,529
Cosine x is the side
to side position of P.

40
00:01:38,929 --> 00:01:40,846
At zero, cosine is one.

41
00:01:40,846 --> 00:01:44,987
It falls to zero at pi by
two, and to minus one at pi.

42
00:01:45,387 --> 00:01:50,023
Then it climbs back, through zero at
three pi by two, to one at two pi.

43
00:01:50,673 --> 00:01:55,038
It is the very same wave, just
slid to the left by pi by two.

44
00:01:55,688 --> 00:01:56,806
Side by side.

45
00:01:56,806 --> 00:02:00,006
The sine wave starts
at the origin, at zero.

46
00:02:00,406 --> 00:02:03,075
The cosine wave starts
at its peak, at one.

47
00:02:03,075 --> 00:02:06,174
Same shape, same height, a
different starting point.

48
00:02:06,774 --> 00:02:07,798
Now you try.

49
00:02:07,798 --> 00:02:11,168
Which graph passes through
the point zero comma one?

50
00:02:11,168 --> 00:02:12,441
Pause and decide.

51
00:02:15,641 --> 00:02:16,541
Cosine!

52
00:02:16,330 --> 00:02:18,805
At x equals zero, cosine is one.

53
00:02:18,805 --> 00:02:22,940
Sine is zero there, so its
graph passes through the origin.

54
00:02:23,590 --> 00:02:25,164
Tangent is wild.

55
00:02:25,164 --> 00:02:28,736
Tangent x is sine x divided by cosine x.

56
00:02:29,136 --> 00:02:33,051
From zero, it climbs slowly at
first, then faster and faster.

57
00:02:33,451 --> 00:02:38,247
As x nears pi by two, cosine nears
zero, and tangent shoots up without

58
00:02:38,247 --> 00:02:39,147
limit.

59
00:02:38,884 --> 00:02:41,423
At pi by two, it is not defined.

60
00:02:42,073 --> 00:02:46,550
Just past pi by two, tangent comes
back from huge negative values.

61
00:02:46,550 --> 00:02:48,077
So the graph breaks.

62
00:02:48,077 --> 00:02:52,728
The dashed line there is an asymptote,
a line the graph gets closer and

63
00:02:52,728 --> 00:02:54,880
closer to, but never touches.

64
00:02:55,530 --> 00:02:59,664
Each piece runs from the bottom to
the top, and a new piece starts every

65
00:02:59,664 --> 00:03:00,564
pi.

66
00:03:00,723 --> 00:03:01,867
Remember this.

67
00:03:01,867 --> 00:03:06,710
Sine starts at zero, cosine starts
at one, and tangent breaks at every

68
00:03:06,710 --> 00:03:08,752
odd multiple of pi by two.

69
00:03:09,452 --> 00:03:10,352
Quick one.

70
00:03:10,347 --> 00:03:15,146
How many times does the sine graph
meet the x axis from zero to two pi,

71
00:03:15,146 --> 00:03:16,567
counting both ends?

72
00:03:16,567 --> 00:03:17,833
Pause and think.

73
00:03:21,033 --> 00:03:21,933
Three!

74
00:03:21,667 --> 00:03:24,194
At zero, at pi, and at two pi.

75
00:03:24,194 --> 00:03:27,678
Those are exactly the
places where sine x is zero.

76
00:03:28,328 --> 00:03:30,063
Now, one worked example.

77
00:03:30,413 --> 00:03:35,229
How many solutions does sine x equals
one half have, from zero to two pi?

78
00:03:35,729 --> 00:03:36,629
Step one.

79
00:03:36,605 --> 00:03:39,533
Draw the sine wave from zero to two pi.

80
00:03:40,283 --> 00:03:41,194
Step two.

81
00:03:41,194 --> 00:03:44,061
Draw the flat line y equals one half.

82
00:03:44,811 --> 00:03:45,711
Step three.

83
00:03:45,652 --> 00:03:47,103
Count where they meet.

84
00:03:47,103 --> 00:03:51,286
The line cuts the upper hump twice,
and never touches the lower half.

85
00:03:52,036 --> 00:03:53,710
So there are two solutions.

86
00:03:53,710 --> 00:03:56,555
The graph gave the count
without solving anything.

87
00:03:57,205 --> 00:03:58,671
Now, the exam trap.

88
00:03:59,021 --> 00:04:03,781
Many students draw tangent as one
long smooth curve, joined across pi by

89
00:04:03,781 --> 00:04:04,681
two.

90
00:04:04,716 --> 00:04:07,538
But tangent is not defined at pi by two.

91
00:04:07,538 --> 00:04:10,804
The graph breaks there,
at a vertical asymptote.

92
00:04:10,804 --> 00:04:12,412
Never join the pieces.

93
00:04:13,062 --> 00:04:14,419
Where is this asked?

94
00:04:14,419 --> 00:04:18,825
In JEE Main, where graphs are used to
count the solutions of an equation.

95
00:04:19,425 --> 00:04:20,654
Exam level now.

96
00:04:20,654 --> 00:04:23,593
How many solutions does
this equation have?

97
00:04:23,593 --> 00:04:24,875
Pause and solve.

98
00:04:30,275 --> 00:04:31,538
The answer is C.

99
00:04:31,538 --> 00:04:32,438
Four.

100
00:04:32,586 --> 00:04:37,469
The modulus of sine x flips the lower
half of the wave up above the axis.

101
00:04:37,969 --> 00:04:42,403
Now there are two humps from zero
to two pi, and both reach up to one.

102
00:04:42,903 --> 00:04:46,279
The line y equals one
half cuts each hump twice.

103
00:04:46,279 --> 00:04:48,253
Two humps, two cuts each.

104
00:04:48,253 --> 00:04:49,416
Four solutions.

105
00:04:50,016 --> 00:04:51,478
Here is your recap.

106
00:04:51,478 --> 00:04:52,981
Screenshot this card.

107
00:04:56,181 --> 00:04:59,018
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

108
00:04:59,418 --> 00:05:00,318
One.

109
00:04:59,879 --> 00:05:03,182
Where does the sine graph
first reach its highest point?

110
00:05:04,082 --> 00:05:04,982
Two.

111
00:05:04,630 --> 00:05:08,518
Which graph is the sine
graph slid left by pi by two?

112
00:05:09,418 --> 00:05:10,318
Three.

113
00:05:10,029 --> 00:05:13,181
Why does the tangent
graph break at pi by two?

114
00:05:14,281 --> 00:05:19,113
Next time: a heartbeat on a monitor
repeats the same shape, over and over.

115
00:05:19,113 --> 00:05:20,507
Sine does that too.

116
00:05:20,507 --> 00:05:22,637
We meet periodicity and symmetry.
